======================================================================
PART 1: EXACT CHEEGER CONSTANT OF THE FLIP GRAPH
======================================================================

  Built flip graph at n=5: 12 classes, 0.3s
  Degrees: [6, 3, 7, 4, 6, 7, 7, 3, 6, 3, 6, 2]

  EXACT Cheeger constant h(G_5) = 1.8333
  Minimizing set S = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 9] (classes [1, 3, 5, 3, 9, 15])
  |S| = 6, |∂S| = 11

  Spectral gap λ₁ = 0.4000
  Cheeger lower bound: λ₁/2 = 0.2000
  Cheeger upper bound: √(2λ₁) = 0.8944
  Actual h = 1.8333
  Gap between actual and lower bound: 1.6333

======================================================================
PART 2: FLIP DISTANCE FROM TRANSITIVE TOURNAMENT
======================================================================

  Flip distance from transitive tournament to each class:
  class |    H | distance |  isoperimetric bound
  ---------------------------------------------
      0 |    1 |        0 |                  0.0
      1 |    3 |        1 |                  0.3
      2 |    5 |        1 |                  0.7
      3 |    3 |        1 |                  0.3
